 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Roughly break the small dead branches first, then light it with a dry brand after it stops sparking. Zigzagging around the base is brave but dumb, wood gives without warning. Yes, in dry conditions. Fill the pocket with coals and switch hands if it' hot. Cotton balls are cheap as well. Stick them in the cold box first, then pull out one as needed. small fire to start, it grows as it burns. Pick a spot, dig a deep fire pit, and set it on top of the ashes. Then fill in and pack it tight.",
